-- An @nlg on its own line above a rule under a section GIVEN.
--
-- Such a rule has no GIVEN of its own: it reads the section's. So it is treated
-- as any rule with no GIVEN, and an @nlg on its own line above its head is its
-- sentence (assumed, not ruled, 2026-11-01, porting legalese/l4-ide#802; the
-- rule for a rule with no GIVEN is main's 98edd9c83). An @nlg indented under the
-- section GIVEN describes the binder and stays the binder's.
--
-- Before the port, the last name in the rule above took the annotation, so
-- `age again` and `seven` read as their bare names.

DECLARE Person HAS
  age IS A NUMBER

§ `Section given`
    GIVEN applicant IS A Person
@nlg the age of the applicant
`applicant age` MEANS applicant's age

@nlg the applicant's age again
`age again` MEANS `applicant age`

§ `Indented under the GIVEN`
    GIVEN claimant IS A NUMBER
          @nlg the claimant's age in years

@nlg the claimant is a minor
`is minor` MEANS claimant < 18

§ `Bare heading`

@nlg the constant seven
seven MEANS 7

#EVAL `applicant age` WITH applicant IS Person 20
#EVAL `age again` WITH applicant IS Person 20
#EVAL `is minor` WITH claimant IS 3
#EVAL seven
